2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2028) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A shared monolith or a single in-memory object model does not hold across those boundaries.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Context and problem statement
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Components in the stack span several languages (C, C++, Python, Elixir, GDScript), run as separate processes, and each binds to hardware, a GPU, the network, or an engine runtime. A component has to stay testable without its device, replaceable without a rewrite of its callers, and composable with components written in another language. A shared monolith or a single in-memory object model does not hold across those boundaries.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Decision drivers
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2028) '- Real-time and pipeline paths cross process and language boundaries with no shared object model.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2028) '- Hardware, OS, GPU, network, and engine concerns have to stay out of the entities and the interactors, or they become untestable away from the live system.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2028) '- CI runs the interactors against recorded data, without the device or the runtime.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2028) '- One computed result often feeds several outputs from a single pass.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Decision outcome
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Each component takes a uniform `entities/` + `repositories/` + `datasources/` layout, in the Netflix formulation of the pattern. Components compose into a service, as RFD66606-2111 defines a service.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2028) '### entities/: the objects, and the interactors that act on them
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2028) 'An entity is an object the component works on, and it knows nothing about where it is stored. An interactor performs the actions on entities. Together they open no socket, read no device, and link no framework. They carry their own `entities/spec/` of tests that run in isolation against recorded data. A transport layer never reaches inside them.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2028) '### repositories/: interfaces to the entities
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A repository is an interface that gets, creates, and changes entities. The interactor declares it and a data source implements it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A repository stays at the lowest common denominator every binding language can implement: a C-ABI struct of function pointers where a service crosses languages, a language-native interface where it does not. One header then binds C, C++, and Python data sources alike.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2028) '### datasources/: the implementations, outside the interactor
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A data source implements a repository against the real world: a serial device, a UDP socket, a recorded fixture for CI, a GPU compute host, a renderer, an engine runtime. One repository admits many data sources, so one pass of an interactor reaches several destinations, and a recorded fixture stands in for live hardware under CI.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2028) '### The transport layer, and composition across the seam
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A transport layer is the input that triggers an interactor. All dependencies point inward, so the transport layer depends on the interactor and never the reverse.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Components compose when a data source of one component is the transport layer of another. An in-process dependency links the sibling directly. A cross-process dependency meets on a wire, which is a protocol the two ends share. The wire is the integration contract, so a producer in one language and a consumer in another share no code, only the message format. Each component declares its sibling wiring beside its repositories.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2028) '- Entities and interactors with no dependencies let CI replay recorded data through them with no device and no runtime.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2028) '- The wire seam decouples languages and processes, so any component is rewritable or replaceable as long as it keeps the message contract.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2028) '- A new output is a new data source, with no change to the interactor that produced the data.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2028) '- All dependencies point inward, so a data source depends on the interactor through a repository, and the interactor depends on nothing.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2028) '- The convention costs interface boilerplate, and across a process boundary it adds a serialize and parse step the in-process link avoids. That cost buys cross-language, cross-process composition.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2028) 'More information
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2028) 'The `sinew-mocap` components apply the pattern end to end. Each git repository (`driver`, `mount_drift`, `solve`, `viewer`, `vr_bridge`) carries the triad. The interfaces are header-only C struct vtables (FrameSource, TrackerSink, PoseSink, HmdSource). The data sources bind the serial dongle, a recorded `.rawlog`, UDP, polyscope, SteamVR, OpenVR, and Vulkan. The components compose over the `/sinew` OSC wire (UDP 39539), and each `sibling-repos.txt` declares the wiring. The synthetic-data branch in `sinew-vrdance/pose_distill` applies the same triad in Python: geometry and label cleaning inside, interfaces for the teacher pose model, the renderer, and the dataset, and data sources for the model, the Godot renderer, and the COCO output.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Those files still carry the older names on disk, and the `*_source.h` / `*_sink.h` spelling with them. RFD66606-2111 holds the rename list.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written
